  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday) \nIssued at 1024 PM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nAs we get into Tuesday, the strong system in New England will start \nto pull off into eastern Canada and open the door for the high \npressure to our southwest to start heading this way. Afternoon \ntemperatures will respond to this increased ridging across the \nregion, warming each day and by Thursday, everyone in the mid-state \nwill be well into the 80s.\n\nAt this point, you're probably asking, what about rain? \nUnfortunately, I don't have any good news in that category for about \na week. In fact, it looks like there's a high likelihood that we \nwill only see a trace of rain at BNA for the entire month of \nSeptember. The last (and only other) time that has occurred on \nrecord was October 1963. The GFS and Euro are fairly consistent \nshowing the mid-week upper ridge slipping to the east and allowing \nfor the return of rain for what looks like a wet weekend next week. \nThe NBM isn't so sure with low rain chances returning Thursday. \nUntil then, enjoy this incredible upcoming weekend.",
